A||N||9||SKIDMARK||V-6 Engine Compartment Wiring Harness?||||5||
Z||000000||SKIDMARK||11-14-2001||11:43 AM||||Is it possible to remove/reinstall the engine & drivetrain in a V-6 with the wiring harness intact? This would mean disconnecting it at the ECM and junction block on the right side of the engine compartment. I have everything apart now and I think it sure would be easier to install all the wiring and accessories on the engine before putting the cradle back in the car. Don't really want to spend a lot of time leaning on my newly painted fenders.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Hank is Here||11-14-2001||11:56 AM||||The harness does disconnect from the ecm.  At the firewall on the interior side there is a clip holdnig the harness to the firewall.  I think it is like a horseshoe clip of something like that.  <BR>So yes you can do what you were saying ||||reg||1
Z||000002||SKIDMARK||11-14-2001||11:59 AM||||All the stupid books I've seen tell you to disconnect everything from the engine and leave the wiring harness in the car. I can't believe this is necessary.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||11-14-2001||12:14 PM||||It's not.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||11-15-2001||07:03 PM||||Looks something like this. . . . . with the harness attached.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSC00013.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||11-15-2001||09:12 PM||||Something like that!? That's exactly what it looks like!||||reg||12
Z||000006||FieroBUZZ||11-15-2001||09:18 PM||||Geez, it looks just like the one in my garage. Except for the red paint, and no rust, and clean wiring wrap, and new parts....oh, well you get the idea.<BR>Gary||||reg||12
Z||000007||tgowens||11-15-2001||10:15 PM||||That's exactly the way we remove the engines from cars at the shop -- disconnect from the ECM, the two joined plugs under the ECM and the ALDL connector and feed through into the engine bay..... remove from the junction block on the right side of the car and remove the two relays and the air filter plug and you are good to go ......... <P>Indiana, I noticed you pulled the a/c compressor along with the engine - I usually remove the a/c compressor bolts and leave it with the car, that way it doesn't discharge the lines making it necessary to recharge the system........ just a thought. Oh, I remove the compressor and hang it with a bungee cord from the deck lid hinge (but then, I remove the engines from the bottom too.......)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||SKIDMARK||11-16-2001||08:47 AM||||Well, mine didn't come out that way but it for sure is going back in with everything on it. I'm learning that I should go with my gut instinct and not always believe the repair manuals. It wasn't easy getting all that stuff off before pulling the cradle.||||reg||6
Z||000009||Indiana_resto_guy||11-16-2001||09:25 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>That's exactly the way we remove the engines from cars at the shop -- disconnect from the ECM, the two joined plugs under the ECM and the ALDL connector and feed through into the engine bay..... remove from the junction block on the right side of the car and remove the two relays and the air filter plug and you are good to go ......... <P>Indiana, I noticed you pulled the a/c compressor along with the engine - I usually remove the a/c compressor bolts and leave it with the car, that way it doesn't discharge the lines making it necessary to recharge the system........ just a thought. Oh, I remove the compressor and hang it with a bungee cord from the deck lid hinge (but then, I remove the engines from the bottom too.......)<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Normally I do hang it, but this is a rebuild/restoration ('88 GT T-TOP) and the A/C compressor is missing from the car. (so was the engine) Thus the reason why . . .<P><p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 11-16-2001).]||||reg||1
